# Authorization & API Contract Rules

## Authorization
- Authentication proves identity; authorization proves scope.
- Every protected command/query must evaluate platform role + tenant scope + customer scope + resource ownership + capability/entitlement.
- Never trust role, tenant, agency, customer or permission identifiers from client state.
- Return non-disclosing authorization/not-found behavior for foreign resources.
- Super Admin is the only role allowed cross-tenant operations, and sensitive overrides require explicit permissions plus audit.

## API design
- Version externally consumed contracts where compatibility matters.
- Validate input at the API boundary and again at domain/application boundaries where invariants matter.
- Do not expose ORM entities directly.
- Use explicit error codes for predictable business failures.
- Pagination/filtering/sorting must have bounded limits.
- Idempotency keys/event IDs are mandatory for sensitive retryable commands.

## Webhooks
Inbound:
- verify signature before parsing sensitive content;
- validate event ID;
- deduplicate before side effects;
- persist receipt/processing status;
- retry safe failures;
- dead-letter poison messages.

Outbound:
- tenant-specific signing secret;
- unique event_id + delivery_id;
- bounded retry/backoff;
- sanitized response metadata;
- replay with explicit authorization;
- no secret-bearing payloads.

## Provider abstraction
Normalize provider responses into Vokit domain/application models.
Do not let provider-specific enums, SDK objects or secrets become the core contract.
